  data:  # dbbf
    kind: work_item  # dbbf
    title: "external_symbol synthesis: stable_id/canonical_name null on every external boundary node; 732 duplicate 'file' nodes on hypergumbo self-analysis"  # dbbf
    status: todo_hard  # dbbf
    priority: 2  # dbbf
    parent:  # dbbf
    tags:  # dbbf
    - analysis_quality  # dbbf
    isbefore: []  # dbbf
    duplicate_of: []  # dbbf
    not_duplicate_of: []  # dbbf
    pr_ref:  # dbbf
    description: "Root-caused from dogfood round 2026-04-24 on `dev` @ f7b3f3f87 (just after the Plan C external_potential merge).\n\n## Symptom\n\n`hypergumbo run .` on hypergumbo itself produces 2,405 `external_symbol` nodes. Of those:\n- 732 named `file`\n- 203 named `module`\n- 38 named `PASS_ID`\n- 25 named `language`\n- 6 named `_is_test_path`\n- etc.\n\nAll 732 \"file\" externals carry distinct `id` fields that embed the referring-site path (e.g. `python:packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/cli.py:1-1:file:file`, `python:packages/hypergumbo-tracker/tests/test_tui.py:1-1:file:file`), but they all share the same null identity metadata: `stable_id=None`, `canonical_name=None`.\n\n## Expected invariant (candidate)\n\nTwo external-boundary `Symbol`s that refer to the same semantic external (same `(module, name)` and source language) should either:\n- (a) deduplicate into a single node, or\n- (b) remain as per-reference nodes but carry a *shared* `stable_id` / `canonical_name` so downstream consumers can group them.\n\nNeither holds today — the synthesis path (WI-sikur, satisfying INV-miniz) emits nodes with `stable_id=None` and `canonical_name=None`.\n\n## Impact\n\n- Inflates node counts on any repo that references common-named stdlib externals. On hypergumbo self-analysis, removing the duplication would drop ~2,000 of the 2,405 external nodes.\n- Breaks cross-run stability that WI-tadof / WI-sapak (ADR-0014 stable_id framework) was supposed to provide for external-boundary symbols.\n- Degrades sketches and slice output by showing hundreds of identical-looking \"file\" nodes from `<external>`.\n- May foul any downstream pass that groups edges by `stable_id` or `canonical_name` of the destination.\n\n## Reproduce\n\n```bash\nhypergumbo run . --out /tmp/hg.json\npython3 -c \"\nimport json\nfrom collections import Counter\nnodes = json.load(open('/tmp/hg.json'))['nodes']\next = [n for n in nodes if (n.get('meta') or {}).get('external_boundary')]\nprint('total:', len(ext))\nfor name, c in Counter(n.get('name') for n in ext).most_common(5):\n    print(f'  {name}: {c}')\nprint('null stable_id:', sum(1 for n in ext if n.get('stable_id') is None))\nprint('null canonical_name:', sum(1 for n in ext if n.get('canonical_name') is None))\n\"\n```\n\n## Likely location\n\nExternal-boundary symbol synthesis is in the pipeline stage that runs after linkers and before serialization (per CHANGELOG [Unreleased] \"External boundary nodes no longer stripped from JSON output — INV-miniz\"). Search for construction of `Symbol` with `kind=\"external_symbol\"` / `meta.external_boundary=True`. The synthesis call site is the fix point.\n\n## Scope expansion (structural-fix protocol)\n\n- Same analysis for `module` (203 copies), `PASS_ID` (38), `language` (25), and other common names.\n- Cross-language: check if JS/TS/Java self-analysis also produces null-stable_id externals.\n- If fix is dedup: ensure `make_typed_stable_id` is called for externals, not just first-party symbols.\n- If fix is canonicalization only: set `canonical_name = f\"{source_lang}:{module}:{name}\"` (or similar) so downstream grouping works.\n\n## Decision to make\n\nBefore implementing, decide whether per-reference external nodes are intentional (so a slice can show \"file is referenced from cli.py line 42\" per site) or whether they should collapse to one node per `(module, name)`. INV-miniz only requires edges to land *somewhere valid* — it doesn't dictate multiplicity."  # dbbf
    fields: {}  # dbbf
