- op: discuss  # 6d12
  at: '2026-04-25T06:59:52Z'  # 6d12
  by: agent  # 6d12
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6d12
  clock: 3  # 6d12
  nonce: 6d12  # 6d12
  message: "Fixed in PR #3355 (commit 1537d03cb) — Plan A (dedupe at synthesis). create_boundary_nodes returns (symbols, id_remap); apply_external_id_remap rewrites edges. file-id pseudo-IDs collapse per language; non-file kinds preserve full path-slot identity. Every boundary Symbol gets stable_id (sha256 of dedupe key) and canonical_name. Tier-min selection across collapsed groups. Self-analysis dogfood: externals 2,405 → 1,514 (~37%); null stable_id/canonical_name 100% → 0%; file-named 732 → 1; 2,152 edges carry referring_paths. Tagged awaits_bakeoff_validation; claim is 'external_symbol count drops on hypergumbo self-analysis; all boundary nodes carry non-null stable_id and canonical_name; per-file attribution survives via meta.referring_paths.'"  # 6d12
- op: discuss  # e177
  at: '2026-04-25T07:05:12Z'  # e177
  by: agent  # e177
  actor: jgstern_agent  # e177
  clock: 4  # e177
  nonce: e177  # e177
  message: "Resolution context (post-merge of PR #3355).\n\n**Plan A vs Plan B — decided.** WI-fozoh's drill-down posed two approaches: dedupe at synthesis (Plan A, narrow scope) vs root-cause structural fix at the producer side (Plan B, multi-PR cross-cutting). Discussion settled on Plan A first (single PR, ~83% of the value, immediate cross-run-stability fix for ALL boundary nodes including non-file ones), with Plan B carved out as a follow-up tracker item: WI-ramuv-gobuf-fagod-gudis-saluh-tofas-tuvud-hiloj. Plan B doesn't need per-analyzer manual inspection of 90+ source files — a centralized post-process at result-collection time handles all affected analyzers in one chokepoint, with an empirical invariant test as the guard.\n\n**Refinement to Plan A during implementation.** The original plan grouped by (language, name, kind), but that collapses too much — ‵urllib.request.urlopen‵ and ‵urllib.parse.urlopen‵ would merge despite being semantically distinct functions. Final shape: dedupe key is (language, path, name, kind) with a special case for ‵kind=\"file\"‵ that drops the per-reference path slot, since file pseudo-IDs carry no semantic identity beyond \"a Python file.\" Result: file externals collapse aggressively (732 → 1 per language); other externals preserve full identity.\n\n**Tier-min selection.** The implementation went with tier-min across collapsed groups (any tier-2 referring site promotes the canonical node) — chosen over the originally-suggested longest-prefix-wins because tier means \"is this declared in our manifests,\" and a single yes shouldn't be silently demoted by a sibling no.\n\n**Self-analysis dogfood verified.** Externals 2,405 → 1,514; null stable_id and canonical_name both 0 (was 100 % each); file-named externals 732 → 1 with id ‵python:<external>:0-0:file:file‵; 2,152 edges carry ‵meta.referring_paths‵ preserving per-file attribution. Tagged ‵awaits_bakeoff_validation‵.\n\n**Known orthogonal issue.** 13 dangling edges remain on hypergumbo self-analysis post-fix — traced to ‵_is_valid_edge_src‵'s permissive ‵.py:‵ fallback at cli.py:6692, which retains edges whose src looks like a Python path even after tier filtering removes the Symbol. Pre-existing; not in WI-fozoh scope. Filing follow-up if it surfaces in future bakeoff cycles."  # e177
